    card title "Which letter is in no state?"

Fifty US states, from Alabama to Wyoming. One of these four letters appears in none of their names.
    draw t_J t_Q t_X t_Z

All four are rare letters in English. But only one is missing completely.
    highlight t_J t_Q t_X t_Z

    ask "Which letter appears in no US state name? Tap it." choose ["t_J","t_Q","t_X","t_Z"] answer t_Q
        right: Q. Not one of the fifty states has a Q in its name.
        wrong: Try spelling the states with the most unusual names.

J is rescued by a single state: New Jersey.
    draw s_J

Z also hangs on by one: Arizona.
    draw s_Z

X does a little better, with Texas and New Mexico.
    draw s_X1 s_X2

But Q has nobody at all.
    draw s_Q

The nearest miss is a cit (@draw abq abq2@)y: Albuquerque, in New Mexico, which has two Qs of its own.

    erase abq abq2

For a Q, you have to c (@draw qc@)ross the border, to the Canadian province of Quebec.

So Q is the only letter of the alphabet that no state name uses.
    highlight t_Q
